From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:35:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(search): a Grok retry when the cheap model reads a
 page but finds no complete size

_extract_dims (role cheap, Groq gpt-oss-20b) gave up on window listings that publish W x H and the
jamb depth only in prose. When its answer is incomplete (or it fails), one more try on role
`extract_retry` (LLM_EXTRACT_RETRY, default xai:grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning; "" = off, and tests
blank it like LLM_FALLBACK). Documented in api.md and the README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
